.TH DEVL 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
devl \- poke the pci_devel_main development driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B devl
.I devnum
.BR hello | ioremap | iounmap
.br
.B devl
.I devnum
.B uint32
.I offset
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens
.BI /dev/pcidev devnum
and issues one ioctl of magic
.BR \(aqD\(aq :
.B IOC_HELLO
(TRACE hello),
.BR IOC_IOREMAP ,
.BR IOC_IOUNMAP ,
or
.B IOC_UINT32
(read the 32-bit register at
.IR offset ).
The value read is reported only through TRACE
.RB ( "val at off=0x%08x" ),
not on stdout unless TRACE slow output is enabled, as
.BR mcs.sh (1)
does with
.BR "tonSg 0\-7" .
The usage also lists
.BR register ,
.B unregister
and
.BR read_loop ,
which are not implemented (TRACE
.BR "invalid cmd" ,
exit 0).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, with no arguments, or for an unimplemented command;
1 if the open or the ioctl fails, or
.B uint32
lacks an offset.
.SH FILES
.BI /dev/pcidev N
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
export TRACE_FILE=/proc/trace/buffer; tonSg 0\-7
devl 0 uint32 0x9004
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcs (1),
.BR mcs.sh (1)
